            "body": "## Summary\n- Removed the always-visible diagnostics `<aside>` panel from `main.tsx`/`styles.css`.\n- Added a warning-presence icon (⚠) to the toolbar's status-indicator area, mutually exclusive with the busy spinner — shown when idle and `view.diagnostics` has entries, hidden otherwise.\n- No warning text/count breakdown in the UI; a hover tooltip shows just the count (e.g. \"3 warnings\").\n- Diagnostic data pipeline (`DesignGraph.diagnostics`, `buildViewModel()`, `postView()`) is untouched, per issue scope.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.webview.json` — passes\n- [x] `npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.extension.json` — passes\n- [x] `npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.cli.json` — passes\n- [x] `CI=true npx vite build` — builds cleanly\n- [x] `npx vitest run` — same pass/fail counts as master (128 pre-existing parser-backend failures unrelated to this change, due to missing compiled backend binary in this environment; verified identical on master before my changes)\n\nCloses #119\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **UI Improvements**\n  * Replaced the inline diagnostics panel with a compact warning indicator.\n  * Warning indicators now display the total diagnostic count through tooltips and accessibility labels.\n  * Updated the layout to position rebuilding and diagnostic status indicators together more cleanly.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
